     "user": "Hollow cylinder, 300 mm diameter, 500 mm tall, 20 mm nozzle, 10 mm layers, 20 s per layer. Fresh density 2150 kg/m3, static yield stress 1.2 kPa, Athix 0.5 Pa/s. Will it stand?",
     "text": "I’ll check plastic collapse and buckling using the buildability calculator, including strength gained between layers.\n**The calculator predicts it will not stand to the target height: plastic collapse governs.**\n\n- Estimated collapse: around **layer 11, at 107 mm**, without a safety factor. With the default **1.5 safety factor**, the limit is about **7 layers**.\n- The build takes **16.7 min**. Calculated base-layer yield stress reaches only **1,700 Pa** by completion.\n- **Cylinder buckling was not evaluated**: the calculator’s buckling check applies to free walls. Open time is also unknown.\n\nTo meet the target with the default safety factor, the calculator requires one of these changes, holding the other inputs fixed:\n\n| Change | Calculated requirement |\n|---|---:|\n| Increase initial static yield stress | ≥8,633 Pa |\n| Increase Athix | ≥7.93 Pa/s |\n| Increase layer cycle time | ≥317 s/layer |\n\nThe slower schedule is conditional on adequate open time and sustained structuration. Accelerator, VMA, or reduced water/binder ratio are possible material adjustments, followed by extrusion and build tests.\n\n**Treat the failure height as a screening estimate.** The closest retrieved [published analogue](https://doi.org/10.1016/j.jobe.2023.106186) recorded collapse at **520 mm**, despite similar rheology; this discrepancy limits confidence in the exact predicted height. Experimental verification is essential.\n\nDefaults used: **23.69 mm filament width**, **1.5 safety factor**; supplied yield stress treated as the value at extrusion. These are deterministic calculations, so prediction quantiles are unavailable.\n\nFiles: [Assessment](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-171139-7c0f/assessment_job.md>), [cycle plot](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-171139-7c0f/cycle_sweep_job.png>), [cycle data](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-171139-7c0f/cycle_sweep_job.csv>), [literature analogues](<C:/Users/User/3D Printing Concrete Prediction/artifacts/reports/agent/20261016-171139-7c0f/similar_prints_job.csv>).\n",
